UPDATE companies SET description='Wisconsin Wire Works, Inc. was founded in 1994 in Wales, Wisconsin, by five copper-industry veterans who set out to produce copper and copper alloy welding wire.

The firm operates as an integrated manufacturer of welding consumables, drawing wire from base stocks sourced from established suppliers. Its facilities house state-of-the-art drawing equipment and an in-house welding laboratory staffed by welding engineers, metallurgists, and fabrication specialists. Products include aluminum bronze, silicon bronze, deoxidized copper, phosphor bronze, copper alloy brazing wires, and nickel aluminum bronze, supplied in precision layer-level wound spools, straightened-and-cut lengths, reels, coils, and barrel packs. All wire undergoes thorough inspection for size, cleanliness, cast, and helix before shipment.

The company serves welders, fabricators, and manufacturers across industries that rely on automatic and robotic welding, with customers on every continent.

Wisconsin Wire Works emphasizes customer-driven quality: drawing dies are reworked on a fixed schedule rather than only when worn, non-contaminating lubricants are used exclusively, and products are cleaned and packed in hermetic moisture-barrier cartons. The quality system is certified to ISO 9001:2000, and the company highlights its made-in-the-USA origin as a core differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2000','ABS']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Copper and copper alloy welding wire manufacturing", "Wire drawing", "Precision layer-level winding", "Straightened-and-cut length production", "Spooling, reeling, coiling, and barrel packing", "In-house welding facility for technical support", "Technical consulting by welding engineers, metallurgists, and fabrication specialists", "Quality inspection (dimensional, cleanliness, cast, helix)", "Drawing die maintenance and rework", "Non-contaminating lubricant application", "Hermetic moisture-barrier packaging", "ISO 9001 quality management"], "industries": ["Welding", "Fabrication", "Manufacturing", "Automatic and robotic welding", "Marine/offshore"], "materials": ["Aluminum Bronze", "Silicon Bronze", "Deoxidized Copper", "Phosphor Bronze", "Copper Alloy Brazing Wires", "Nickel Aluminum Bronze", "Copper", "Copper alloys"], "equipment": ["Wire drawing equipment", "Drawing dies"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Precision layer-level wound spools for reliable feeding in automatic and robotic welding", "Drawing dies reworked on a regular preventive schedule to maintain surface quality", "Thorough inspection program covering size, cleanliness, cast, and helix on every lot", "Exclusive use of non-contaminating lubricants and hermetic moisture-barrier packaging", "ISO 9001:2000 and ABS certified quality system"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1994 by five copper-industry veterans -> db", "Headquarters in Wales, Wisconsin -> db", "Integrated manufacturer of copper and copper alloy welding wire -> /", "Current leadership: John Turriff (President/Owner), Tressa Turriff (VP), Ryan Turriff (VP), Jeremy Hoadley (Sales Manager) -> /", "State-of-the-art drawing equipment, regular die rework -> /", "Inspection program for size, cleanliness, cast, helix -> /", "Non-contaminating lubricants, thorough cleaning, hermetic moisture-barrier packaging -> /", "Products: aluminum bronze, silicon bronze, deoxidized copper, phosphor bronze, copper alloy brazing wires, nickel aluminum bronze -> /", "Product forms: precision layer-level wound spools, straightened-and-cut lengths, reels, coils, barrel packs -> /", "In-house welding facility, technical support by welding engineers, metallurgists, fabrication specialists -> /", "ISO 9001:2000 certification (Certificate Number A2541US) -> /", "ABS certified supplier -> /", "Customers on every continent -> /", "Serves welders, fabricators, manufacturers, automatic/robotic welding applications -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Wisconsin Wire Works Inc. is an integrated manufacturer of copper and copper alloy welding wire.", "founded_year": "1994", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wisconsin-wire-works-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Wise Plastics Technologies, headquartered in St. Charles, Illinois, traces its roots to 1974 when it was founded as Wise‑Hamlin Plastics in the greater Chicagoland area.

The molder runs over 100 injection presses ranging from 35 to 1,100 tons, supporting custom plastic injection molding, two‑shot, insert and over‑molding, in‑mold labeling, and liquid silicone rubber (LSR) molding for medical‑grade and biocompatible applications. Value‑added operations include assembly, sonic welding, heat staking, printing, decorating, packaging and kitting. Engineering services cover design for manufacturing, rapid prototyping, mold design and build, process optimization and failure analysis. The quality lab provides first‑article inspection, capability studies, IQ/OQ/PQ, PPAP and CMM inspection, with scientific molding processes monitored 24/5 and 24/7 when demand requires.

Wise Plastics serves the medical device and pharmaceutical sectors, holding ISO 13485:2016 certification for medical‑device quality management, and is ITAR registered for defense‑related work. The company also supports a range of other industries through its supply‑chain management, inventory and logistics programs.

Founded on a vision to provide reliable, high‑quality injection molding partnerships, Wise Plastics emphasizes purpose‑built facilities, integrated manufacturing operations, advanced automation on every cell, and a team of 200‑plus skilled employees who operate around the clock. Its quality system is certified to ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 13485:2016, and the firm holds OSHA SHARP recognition for safety.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ISO 13485:2016','ITAR Registered','OSHA SHARP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic Injection Molding", "Two-shot Injection Molding", "Insert Molding", "Over-Molding", "In-Mold Labeling (IMD/IML)", "RJG Scientific Molding", "Decoupled Molding\u00ae Processes", "Liquid Silicone Rubber (LSR) Molding", "Medical Grade LSR", "Clean Room Manufacturing", "Tooling Transfers (Domestic and International)", "Tool Refurbishment & Repair", "Contract Manufacturing (Turnkey)", "Design for Manufacturing (DFM)", "Rapid Prototyping", "Mold Design & Build", "Process Optimization", "Material Selection", "Failure Analysis", "Assembly Services", "Sonic Welding", "Heat Staking", "Printing & Decorating", "Packaging Solutions"], "industries": ["Medical Device", "Pharmaceutical", "Defense"], "materials": ["Medical-grade thermoplastics", "Liquid silicone rubber (LSR)", "Biocompatible materials", "High-temperature resistant materials"], "equipment": ["100+ injection presses (35\u20131,100 ton)", "RJG scientific molding systems", "Decoupled Molding\u00ae processes", "CMM inspection equipment", "Automated part handling systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO 9001:2015 and ISO 13485:2016 certified quality management", "RJG scientific molding with automation on every press cell", "200+ skilled employees running 24/5 and 24/7 as needed", "Three purpose\u2011built Illinois facilities with 350,000+ sq ft capacity", "Full supply\u2011chain management including sourcing, inventory and logistics"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1974 as Wise-Hamlin Plastics -> /about", "Headquarters St. Charles, Illinois -> /about, /", "Three facilities, 350,000+ sq ft -> /about, /", "100+ presses 35-1100 tons -> /, /services", "200+ skilled employees -> /, /about", "ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, ITAR, OSHA SHARP -> /, /about", "Capabilities: injection molding, two-shot, insert, over-molding, LSR, scientific molding, automation -> /services", "Value-added: assembly, sonic welding, heat staking, printing, packaging, kitting -> /services", "Engineering services: DFM, prototyping, mold design, process optimization -> /services", "Quality services: first article, capability studies, IQ/OQ/PQ, PPAP, CMM -> /services", "Industries: Medical & Pharmaceutical, ITAR for defense -> /, /services, /about", "Purpose-built facilities, integrated operations, automation, 24/7 production -> /about, /", "Vision: reliable high-quality injection molding partnerships -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Wise Plastics Technologies is a full turnkey contract manufacturing company headquartered in St. Charles, Illinois \u2014 only 30 minutes from Chicago and O''Hare \u2014 specializing in custom plastic injection molding, liquid silicone injection molding (LSR), and value-added secondary operations.", "founded_year": "1974", "employee_count": "200+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wise-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='WishBone Medical, Inc. is a pediatric orthopedic company based in Warsaw, Indiana. The company focuses on the unmet needs of children suffering from orthopedic issues, aiming to provide anatomically appropriate solutions for growing patients.

The company designs and manufactures anatomically appropriate implants and instruments, delivered in single-use, sterile-packed procedure kits. Its product lines include growth control systems, plating systems, and bone void fillers. Kits are assembled with multi-barrier sterile packaging and include web-based software for precise correction in all planes. All instruments are supplied sharp and pristine for each procedure, eliminating the need for loaner trays and reducing operating room turnover time.

WishBone Medical serves pediatric orthopedic surgeons and hospitals, providing kits that streamline procedural efficiency and reduce overall patient care costs. Its customers include medical facilities that perform pediatric orthopedic surgeries.

