UPDATE companies SET description='Wolf Hill Technologies operates from Nashville, Tennessee, providing residential and commercial technology installation services. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed in available sources.

The firm specializes in the installation, networking, and maintenance of smart home technology, home theater systems, security and surveillance systems, and audio and surround sound solutions. It also handles conference hall and event center installations, including wired and wireless sound, video, and security systems. Services cover both new installations and ongoing technical support for homes and businesses.

Customers include homeowners seeking whole-home automation, multi-zone audio, and remote security access, as well as commercial clients such as offices, venues, and event centers requiring integrated audio-visual and security infrastructure. The company emphasizes scalable solutions tailored to budget and objectives.

Wolf Hill Technologies highlights its use of user-friendly, multi-use control devices that consolidate system management, along with a focus on affordable, state-of-the-art technology and responsive technical service and maintenance.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Smart home technology installation and networking", "Home theater design and installation", "Security system and surveillance installation", "Audio and surround sound installation", "Conference hall and event center AV installation", "Closed-circuit TV installation and setup", "Wireless and wired system integration", "Technical service and maintenance"], "industries": ["Residential technology integration", "Commercial audio-visual installation", "Security systems integration", "Event venue technology"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single-device control for entire home or business systems", "Remote security access via smartphone, tablet, or computer", "Installation and maintenance for conference halls and event centers", "Customized home theater and multi-zone audio packages"], "facts_used": ["Location: Nashville, Tennessee -> db", "Services: smart home, home theater, security, audio, conference halls -> page /", "Phone:  -> page /", "Remote access via smartphone/tablet/computer -> page /", "User-friendly multi-use control devices -> page /", "Maintenance and technical service offered -> page /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Wolf Hill Technologies provides residential and commercial installation for home theaters, security systems, audio and surround sound, and full home automation", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wolf-hill-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Wolf Metals operates from Columbus, Ohio, where it was founded in 1974 by Jim and Mike Wolf. The family-owned business began as a small local shop and has grown into a custom metal fabrication specialist serving customers nationwide.

The company provides a full range of fabrication services including laser cutting, water jet cutting, forming, shearing, MIG and TIG welding, fastener insertion, powder coating, plating, assembly, CNC machining, leveling, tube laser cutting, laser welding, and aluminum composite material (ACM) panel fabrication. Its 100,000-square-foot facility houses more than 50 state-of-the-art machines, enabling production runs from single prototypes to high-volume orders.

Wolf Metals serves the automotive, aerospace, defense, energy, medical, agriculture, construction, and industrial machinery sectors. A recent project involved engineering a modular aluminum exoskeleton for DTi Creative to transform John Deere Gators into performance vehicles for marching bands.

