re values: uncompromising quality, innovation, customer focus, integrity, teamwork -> /about-us", "End-to-end solutions under one roof -> /about-us", "Volume range: one-off custom pieces to large production runs -> /about-us", "Founders: Jim Wolf (Founder & CEO), Mike Wolf (Operations Manager), Pat Wolf (Equipment Operator) -> /about-us", "Address: 1625 W Mound St, Columbus, OH 43223 -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "From design and prototyping to production and finishing, we offer end-to-end solutions under one roof.", "founded_year": "1974", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wolf-metals' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Wolfe Custom Woodworking LLC operates from Englewood, Colorado, serving the Denver metropolitan area. The company was founded by Daniel E. Wolfe, who has spent many years crafting fine furniture and cabinets before establishing the LLC.

The shop provides full-service design, fabrication, and installation of built-in cabinetry, shelving, and stand-alone hardwood tables and casework. Projects range from custom banquettes and dining tables to media credenzas, bookshelves, hutches, and side tables. Work is executed using traditional joinery techniques such as bowtie joints and hand-carved bevels, with each piece designed and fabricated by Wolfe himself. Materials include white oak, North American black walnut, Indian rosewood, and vinyl for casework applications.

Past projects include a white oak banquette and dining table, a walnut banquette, a mid-century modern media credenza, a solid walnut bookshelf, a shaker hutch, and a modern side table featuring a bookmatched Indian rosewood top. A client testimonial describes a custom walnut barn door for a master bathroom.

Wolfe emphasizes direct client involvement in the design process, believing that custom work should reflect each customer’s exact vision. He cites a passion for creating pieces that clients will use and love for years, and differentiates the shop by personally handling every stage of design and fabrication.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cabinetry design and fabrication", "Built-in cabinetry installation", "Stand-alone hardwood furniture making", "Custom shelving fabrication", "Casework fabrication", "Joinery (bowtie joints, hand-carved bevel)", "Design consultation", "Project installation"], "industries": [], "materials": ["White Oak", "North American Black Walnut", "Indian Rosewood", "Vinyl", "Hardwood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full-service design, fabrication, and installation under one roof", "Every project built personally by the founder", "Client collaboration encouraged throughout the design process", "Specialization in built-in cabinetry and stand-alone hardwood furniture", "Local service focus on the Denver Metro Area"], "facts_used": ["Company name and location (Englewood, CO) -> db", "Founder: Daniel E. Wolfe -> /about-us", "Services: design, fabrication, installation of built-in cabinetry, shelving, hardwood tables, casework -> /, /about-us", "Materials: White Oak, North American Black Walnut, Indian Rosewood, Vinyl -> /services", "Processes: custom woodworking, joinery (bowtie joints, hand-carved bevel) -> /services, /about-us", "Project examples: White Oak Banquette & Dining Table, Vinyl Casework, Walnut Banquette, Mid Century Modern Media Credenza, Solid Walnut Bookshelf, Shaker Hutch, Modern Side Table -> /services", "Client testimonial: custom walnut barn door for master bathroom -> /", "Ownership: LLC under Daniel Wolfe -> /, /about-us", "Service area: Denver Metro Area -> /, /about-us", "Differentiators: personal fabrication, client design collaboration, passion for lasting products -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Wolfe Custom Woodworking LLC is a full service design, fabrication and installation shop serving the Denver Metro Area. We focus primarily on creating built-in cabinetry, shelving, and stand alone hardwood tables and casework.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wolfe-custom-woodworking-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Wood Components & Technologies operates from Cedar Falls, Iowa. The business evolved from a producer of wood bearings for agricultural equipment and washing machines into a manufacturer of wood and plastic OEM parts for a range of industries.

The company produces curved and arched moldings, lineal trim, and specialty millwork for commercial contractors and home builders. It also machines wood and plastic OEM components for manufacturers of machinery equipment. CNC machining is a core process used for custom millwork, including arched windows, doors, and handrails.

Its customer base includes architects, building centers, contractors, and homeowners in the commercial and residential construction sectors, as well as manufacturers of agricultural equipment and appliances. A featured project for Jokers Comedy Club in Cedar Falls highlights custom arch windows, custom doors, and machined handrail.

The firm’s focus on wood and plastic OEM parts for machinery equipment reflects a deliberate shift toward serving industrial manufacturers alongside the architectural millwork market.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Curved and arched millwork", "Lineal millwork", "CNC machining", "OEM parts manufacturing", "Custom millwork", "Machined handrails", "Specialty millwork"], "industries": ["Commercial construction", "Residential construction", "Machinery equipment manufacturing", "Agricultural equipment", "Appliance manufacturing"], "materials": ["Wood", "Plastic"], "equipment": ["CNC routers"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["CNC machining for custom curved and arched millwork", "Wood and plastic OEM parts for machinery equipment", "Specialty millwork for commercial and residential projects", "Historical expertise in wood bearings for agriculture and appliance industries"], "facts_used": ["Location: Cedar Falls, Iowa -> db", "Products: curved and arched moldings, lineal trim, specialty millwork, wood and plastic OEM parts -> /", "Processes: CNC machining -> /", "Industries served: commercial contractors, home builders, machinery equipment manufacturers -> /", "Example project: Jokers Comedy Club custom arch windows, doors, machined handrail -> /", "History: shifted from wood bearings for agriculture equipment and washing machines to wood OEM parts -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Wood Components offers quality curved and arched moldings, lineal trim, and specialty millwork for commercial contractors and home builders, plus wood and plastic OEM parts and components for manufacturers of machinery equipment.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wood-components-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='American Woods traces its roots to 1979 when Wood Products Inc. began as a cabinet shop serving Innes Construction in Grand Forks, North Dakota. The business expanded into commercial cabinetry, and in 1982 Lowell and Georgia Innes founded American Woods to meet customer demand for matching hardwood accessories. The two entities merged under the American Woods name in 2003, combining custom cabinetry with a growing line of wood goods under single ownership.

Today the company operates a roughly 160,000-square-foot furniture manufacturing facility in Grand Forks with a workforce of about 100. The plant runs milling, machining, sanding, sawing, sub-assembly, finishing, and final assembly lines, producing a wide range of home furnishing products from real hardwoods and premium materials. Daily truck shipments move finished goods to distribution points across the country.

American Woods supplies finished furniture to multiple nationally recognized brands, including long-standing partner Room & Board (producing the Berkeley, Copenhagen, and Danbury lines) and former mass-market programs for Target, Costco, and Lowe''s. The company also works directly with resellers seeking luxury furniture solutions and maintains its own branded collections.

The business emphasizes American-made craftsmanship, consistency, and efficiency, framing its differentiation around enduring partnerships, a made-in-America promise, and a team culture built on pride and integrity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Milling", "Machining", "Sanding", "Sawing", "Sub-assembly", "Finishing", "Final assembly", "Daily truck shipment coordination"], "industries": ["Furniture manufacturing", "Home furnishings", "Outdoor furniture", "Cabinetry", "Retail", "Luxury furniture"], "materials": ["Hardwoods", "Cedar", "Premium materials"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Made in America, built to last", "Daily truck shipments for consistent nationwide delivery", "100-person team covering every production stage from milling to final assembly", "Long-term partnerships with national brands such as Room & Board, Target, Costco, and Lowe''s", "Single-site operation merging custom cabinetry and branded furniture lines"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 by Lowell and Georgia Innes in Grand Forks, ND -> /about-us", "Wood Products Inc started 1979 as cabinet shop for Innes Construction -> /about-us", "Merged 2003 under American Woods name -> /about-us", "Facility ~160,000 sq ft -> /about-us", "100-person team -> /about-us", "Processes: milling, machining, sanding, sawing, sub-assembly, finishing, final assembly -> /about-us", "Daily truck shipments -> /about-us", "Partnership with Room & Board since 2001 -> /about-us", "Supplied Target, Costco, Lowes -> /about-us", "Materials: real hardwoods, cedar, premium materials -> /about-us", "Leadership team names -> /about-us", "Company values: grit, innovation, people -> /", "Luxury furniture focus -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our furniture manufacturing facility spans approximately 160,000 square feet and is equipped to produce a wide range of high-quality home furnishing products.", "founded_year": "1982", "employee_count": "50-100", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='wood-products-inc-dba-american-woods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Wood Products Northwest Inc. operates from Ellensburg, Washington, where it was founded in 1989. The company began when its CEO identified a gap between industry needs and the limited supply of custom cabinet manufacturers in the region.

The shop produces custom cabinetry for residential kitchens, bathrooms, and offices, as well as commercial casework and countertops. Its capabilities span custom cabinetry, commercial casework, and countertop fabrication, though facility size, headcount, and annual volumes are not disclosed.

The company serves both residential and commercial construction markets, supplying cabinets and casework for remodel and new-build projects. Its supply chain includes partnerships with major hardware and surface brands such as Blum, Formica, Wilsonart, and Sherwin-Williams, among others.

