UPDATE companies SET description='Woodtech, a division of Datatek, was launched in early 2014 in Huntsville, Alabama. Datatek traces its roots to 1988 when it began as Alabama Blueprint & Supply Co., Inc., producing blue line prints for architects and engineers. Woodtech emerged to combine digital printing with fine woodworking, opening a retail showroom in the Clinton Row project downtown.

Woodtech operates a production facility offering CNC woodworking, digital flatbed printing, and custom finishing. Services include custom signage, furniture, inlays, overlays, framing, and polyurethane coating. The shop sources reclaimed lumber from Madison County and North Alabama, partnering with local artists for design input. A partnership with Swampworks Amplifiers adds custom-built, printed amplifiers to the lineup. The facility supports both one-off custom pieces and repeat production runs.

Customers span construction, architecture, engineering, real estate, fine art, photography, education, and brewing industries. The company serves businesses needing jobsite signs, presentation boards, retail-ready home décor, gift items, and custom furniture build-outs. Local breweries, schools, and retail shops are cited as repeat clients.

Woodtech emphasizes a local supply chain, using wood from naturally felled trees and collaborating with regional artists. The division was started to merge digital printing capabilities with woodworking, creating customizable yet scalable products. The downtown showroom provides a direct retail channel while the production side serves B2B orders.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC woodworking", "Digital flatbed printing", "Custom signage production", "Custom furniture manufacturing", "Custom framing", "Polyurethane coating application", "Reclaimed wood sourcing", "Custom amplifier assembly (partnered)"], "industries": ["Construction", "Architecture", "Engineering", "Real estate", "Fine art", "Photography", "Education", "Food and beverage (breweries)", "Home d\u00e9cor", "Gift retail", "Furniture", "Retail"], "materials": ["Wood", "Reclaimed wood", "Plywood", "Polyurethane", "Various signage substrates"], "equipment": ["Digital flatbed printer", "CNC router"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Oldest full-service reprographic company in the region (since 1988)", "Local art and photography partnerships for product designs", "Wood sourced from North Alabama reclaimed timber", "Digital flatbed printing combined with fine woodworking", "Retail showroom in downtown Huntsville''s Clinton Row"], "facts_used": ["Woodtech division launched in early 2014 -> /about-us", "Parent company Datatek founded 1988 as Alabama Blueprint & Supply Co., Inc. -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Huntsville, Alabama -> db", "Offers CNC woodworking services -> /about-us", "Uses digital flatbed printer for custom signage -> /about-us", "Sources reclaimed wood from Madison County and North Alabama -> /about-us", "Partners with local artists and photographers for designs -> /about-us", "Operates retail showroom in Clinton Row downtown -> /about-us", "Applies polyurethane coating for moisture protection -> capabilities", "Partnered with Swampworks Amplifiers for custom printed amps -> products"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We could produce unique, customizable products that could still be mass produced.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='woodtech' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Woodworking Masters, a family-owned woodworking shop, was founded in 1996 in Pacoima, California.

The company produces custom doors, stairs and balusters, and engineered wood veneers, supported by in-house shop milling services. Designs are developed using CAD software, and each piece undergoes a final inspection before delivery.

Woodworking Masters serves homeowners, general contractors, and interior designers primarily in the Los Angeles area.

The founders emphasize that every piece of wood has a story, and they cite over 30 years of combined craftsmanship as the foundation of their quality standards. The shop’s differentiation rests on material selection, attention to detail, and a design-to-build workflow that integrates CAD precision with hand-finished artistry.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Shop milling", "Custom door manufacturing", "Stair and baluster fabrication", "Wood veneer engineering", "CAD design", "Quality inspection"], "industries": ["Residential construction", "Interior design", "Architectural millwork"], "materials": ["Wood (various species)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 30 years of woodworking experience", "Family-owned and operated", "CAD-driven design and precision manufacturing", "Works with all wood species", "Custom handmade architectural woodwork"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1996 -> db", "Headquarters in Pacoima, California -> db", "Family-owned -> /about", "Custom doors, stairs, veneer, shop milling -> /", "CAD design -> /", "Serves homeowners, contractors, designers -> /about", "Over 30 years experience -> /about", "Works with all wood types -> /about", "Contact names Anthony Aguirre, Leo Aguinaga, Antonio Aguirre -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Based in Los Angeles, CA, we are a family-owned Woodworking Shop that is dedicated to crafting custom handmade woodworks for our customers.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='woodworking-masters' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Woodworks Distilling Co. operates from Oklahoma City, Oklahoma, where founders Dave Wood and David Alexander launched the craft distillery after years of experience in retail, warehousing, and the brewing industry. Wood, the CEO, had long envisioned the venture, while Alexander brings expertise as a chemist, regulatory specialist, and cocktail designer. The company does not disclose a founding year or ownership structure such as family or veteran status.

The distillery produces a range of spirits including 100% corn vodka distilled six times, a four-grain vodka, dry and barrel-aged gins, sourced bourbon and rye whiskeys under the Preface Series, and corn-based liqueurs such as Apple Pie Corn Liquor through its Horns Down Fine Spirits partnership. Emphasis is placed on small batches, local ingredients, and wood influence throughout aging and flavor development. Facility size, headcount, and annual volumes are not publicly specified.

The company also operates an event space at its Britton Road location, hosting weddings, live music, chef dinners, and private functions managed by Front of House Manager Abbey Elliot.

