UPDATE companies SET description='Founded in Taiwan in 1985 as a monitor cable specialist, Y.C. Cable entered the U.S. OEM market in 1991 and established Y.C. Cable USA Inc. in Fremont, California, in 1997. The company is headquartered in Fremont, California.

Y.C. Cable manufactures custom cable assemblies and wire harnesses, offering processes that include wire cutting, stripping, crimping, solder termination, connector assembly, harness assembly, shielding, overmolding, heat-shrink application, labeling, and electrical testing. The company operates globally with locations in Fremont, Irvine, and Piscataway in the United States, as well as New Taipei City, Taiwan, and Dongguan, China, supporting prototype, NPI, build-to-print, and repeat production.

The company serves OEMs in AI and data centers, automation and robotics, medical and healthcare equipment, automotive electronics, consumer electronics, industrial equipment, and telecom and communications. Examples include high-speed, high-density cables for GPU servers; high-flex cables for robotic arms; medical diagnostic and monitoring equipment cables; automotive sensor, lighting, and infotainment harnesses; and USB Type-C and Lightning cables for consumer devices.

Y.C. Cable emphasizes its end-to-end NPI process, which moves programs from engineering design review and DFM through component sourcing, production planning, inspection, and final testing. The company highlights its multi-site quality certifications—including ISO 9001, ISO 13485, IATF 16949, ISO 14001, and ISO 45001—and its ability to support both quick-turn prototypes and high-volume manufacturing under customer-approved documentation.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 14001','ISO 45001','ISO 13485','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire and cable cutting", "Stripping and preparation", "Crimping", "Solder termination", "Connector assembly", "Wire harness assembly", "Shield preparation and termination", "Protective sleeving", "Heat-shrink application", "Overmolding", "Molded strain relief", "Labeling and identification", "Electrical testing", "Pinout verification", "Visual inspection", "Dimensional inspection", "Customer-defined testing", "Engineering design review & DFM", "BOM integration & project planning", "Component sourcing and line allocation", "Production, inspection & testing", "Final testing & delivery", "Quick-turn prototyping", "Build-to-print manufacturing", "Contract wire harness manufacturing", "PCBA & cable assembly services"], "industries": ["AI & Data Centers", "Automation & Robotics", "Medical & Healthcare Equipment", "Automotive", "Consumer Electronics", "Industrial", "Telecom & Communications"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Small-volume quick-turn prototypes to high-volume manufacturing", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["End-to-end NPI support from prototype through repeat production", "Global manufacturing footprint across U.S. and Asia", "Multi-certification quality systems (ISO 9001, ISO 13485, IATF 16949, ISO 14001, ISO 45001)", "Engineering and DFM support for manufacturability review", "Quick-turn prototyping and first-article builds"], "facts_used": ["Founded in Taiwan in 1985 -> /about", "Entered U.S. OEM market in 1991 -> /about", "Y.C. Cable USA Inc. established in Fremont, California in 1997 -> /about", "Headquartered in Fremont, California -> /about", "Manufactures custom cable assemblies and wire harnesses -> /", "Processes: wire cutting, stripping, crimping, solder termination, connector assembly, harness assembly, shielding, overmolding, heat-shrink, labeling, electrical testing -> /about", "Global locations: Fremont, Irvine, Piscataway, New Taipei City, Dongguan -> /about", "Industries served: AI & Data Centers, Automation & Robotics, Medical, Automotive, Consumer Electronics, Industrial, Telecom & Communications -> /about", "NPI process: engineering design review, DFM, component sourcing, production planning, inspection, testing -> /", "Certifications: ISO 9001, ISO 13485, IATF 16949, ISO 14001, ISO 45001 -> /about", "Supports quick-turn prototypes to high-volume manufacturing -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Y.C. Cable manufactures custom cable assemblies and wire harnesses for OEM applications", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='y-c-cable-yc-cable-usa' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='YMI Industries was founded in 1947 in Grand Forks, North Dakota, and has remained a family-owned business throughout its history. The company began with a focus on producing tool and die components for metalworking, establishing a customer base that has spanned decades.

Today the shop provides a broad range of metal fabrication and machining services, including laser cutting, metal stamping, CNC press brake bending, tool and die design and repair, welding and fabrication, CNC turning, and CNC milling with in‑house heat treating. The facility operates CNC lathes, multiple press brakes, laser cutting systems, and coordinate measuring machines for inspection, supporting work from rapid prototyping through production runs.

YMI serves original equipment manufacturers, innovators, and other organizations in the metalworking sector that require precision components and tooling. Customers rely on the company for both one‑off prototypes and repeat production of stamped, formed, and machined parts.

The company’s guiding principle, "Making Response to Customers a Top Priority Since 1947," reflects its emphasis on communication, on‑time delivery, and competitive pricing. An ISO 9001‑certified quality system, backed by CMM inspection and a commitment to resolving non‑conformities quickly, underpins that promise.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser cutting", "Metal stamping", "Press brake bending", "Tool and die design, production, and repair", "Welding and fabrication", "CNC turning", "CNC machining", "Prototyping", "Design and engineering (via partners)", "Finishing (via partners)"], "industries": ["Metalworking", "OEM manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CNC lathes", "CNC press brakes", "Laser cutting machines", "Coordinate measuring machines (CMM)", "Go/no-go gauges"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Customer response prioritized since 1947 (company motto)", "Family-owned continuity since 1947", "ISO 9001 certified quality management system", "In-house heat treating capability", "CMM-based inspection and go/no-go gauging"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1947 -> db", "Family-owned since 1947 -> /about", "Headquarters Grand Forks, North Dakota -> db", "ISO 9001 certified -> db, /, /quality", "Services: laser cutting, metal stamping, press brake bending, tool & die, welding & fabrication, turning machining, CNC machining, prototyping, custom services -> /services", "Equipment: CNC lathes, CNC press brakes, laser cutting machines, CMM, go/no-go gauges -> /services, /quality", "Industries: OEM manufacturers, innovators, organizations in metalworking -> /about, description", "Motto: Making Response to Customers a Top Priority Since 1947 -> /, /about", "In-house heat treating -> /services (CNC Machining section)", "One-stop shop with partner network for design, engineering, finishing -> /services (Custom Services)"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "produce tool and die components for metalworking", "founded_year": "1947", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ymi-industries' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
