UPDATE companies SET description='Zero Manufacturing is headquartered in North Salt Lake, Utah, and traces its origins to 1931 when German immigrant Herman Zierold established a small sheet-metal shop in Los Angeles after designing a rugged aluminum case to protect his engineering documents in the California oil fields. The business evolved through several ownership changes and was later renamed Zero Manufacturing Co. in 1959. Today the company operates under the leadership of Rockwood Equity Partners and CEO Declan McLaughlin.

The company specializes in mission-critical protective cases and enclosures made from high-strength aluminum and advanced polymers. Its 286,000-square-foot Utah facility houses deep-drawn aluminum forming, rotomolding, laser cutting, CNC punching, certified welding, anodizing, powder coating, and assembly operations. With 145 team members, Zero produces more than 270,000 parts annually across 2,600 unique SKUs and has manufactured over 5 million products since inception.

Zero serves aerospace and aviation, defense and military, medical, energy/oil & gas, industrial, electronics & infrastructure, and logistics sectors. Its cases have protected equipment ranging from Apollo 11 moon-rock containers to avionics, field-deployed medical diagnostics, and downhole sensors in harsh oilfield environments. Customers include NASA, major defense contractors, medical device OEMs, and industrial equipment manufacturers.

Zero positions itself as an engineering-led manufacturing partner that combines disciplined engineering, vertically controlled domestic production, and long-term partnership. The company emphasizes predictable lead times, consistent quality through ISO 9001-certified processes, and expert guidance from concept through testing — often at no cost — to deliver protection where failure is not an option.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Aluminum Laser Cutting", "Trumpf TruPunch Press", "Deep Drawn Aluminum", "Aluminum & Metal Anodizing", "Painting & Powdercoating", "Certified Welding", "Custom Tooling", "Rotomolding Plastic", "Standard & Custom Assembly", "Precision Machining", "Surface Finishing", "Tooling & Forming"], "industries": ["Aerospace", "Aviation", "Defense", "Military", "Medical", "Energy, Oil & Gas", "Industrial", "Electronics & Infrastructure", "Logistics"], "materials": ["Aluminum", "Advanced polymers", "Plastic"], "equipment": ["Trumpf TruPunch Press"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fully domestic manufacturing in a 286,000 sq. ft. Utah facility", "Vertically controlled production from engineering to final assembly", "Engineering-led design partnership offered at no cost", "Deep-drawn aluminum and rotomolded plastic capabilities under one roof"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1931 -> db", "HQ North Salt Lake, Utah -> db", "Employee count 145 -> db", "ISO 9001 certification -> db", "Facility size 286,000 sq ft -> /", "Parts produced annually 270,000+ -> /", "Unique SKUs 2,600 -> /", "Customer base 3,100 -> /", "Products manufactured 5,000,000 -> /", "Founder Herman Zierold -> /about-us", "Origins 1929 -> /about-us", "Rockwood Equity Partners ownership -> /about-us", "CEO Declan McLaughlin -> /about-us", "Apollo 11 moon rock cases -> /about-us", "Deep-drawn aluminum and rotomolded plastic -> /about-us", "Capabilities list -> /capabilities", "Industries served -> /capabilities", "Trumpf TruPunch Press -> /", "Aluminum Laser Cutting -> /", "Painting & Powdercoating -> /", "Certified Welding -> /", "Custom Tooling -> /", "Rotomolding Plastic -> /", "Standard & Custom Assembly -> /", "Surface Finishing -> /", "Tooling & Forming -> /", "Aluminum & Metal Anodizing -> /", "Precision Machining -> /", "Materials: high-strength aluminum and advanced polymers -> /", "Industries: Aerospace, Aviation, Defense, Military, Medical, Energy, Oil & Gas, Industrial, Electronics & Infrastructure, Logistics -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Precision-built in our fully domestic facility, Zero ensures consistent quality through controlled processes, advanced fabrication, and superior materials.", "founded_year": "1931", "employee_count": "145", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='zero-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Zell Manufacturing Company Inc. operates from Export, Pennsylvania, about 25 miles east of Pittsburgh. The company was founded in 1965 in Wilkinsburg by Clifford R. Zell and moved to its current location shortly after. It remains a family-owned business, now led by Clifford’s sons and grandchildren.

The shop produces wooden and plastic components, custom moldings, and CNC-machined parts. Its 9,000-square-foot facility houses fully automated machinery and custom molding equipment, including a five-cutter-head molder. Capabilities span cutting (cross-cuts, rip cuts, custom cuts), drilling, planing, shaping, sanding, finishing (clear coats, paints, stains, silk screening, wood burning), miter and box jointing, assembly, packaging, and shipping.

Customers come from construction, point-of-purchase advertising, furniture, consumer goods, architecture, interior design, manufacturing, and toy industries. The company serves both individual buyers and large corporations, offering custom packaging and fulfillment services that cover inventory management, order processing, and shipping logistics.

