UPDATE companies SET description='Zenith Electronics LLC is headquartered in Lincolnshire, Illinois. Founded in 1918, the company began with the advent of radio. Since 1999, it has operated as a wholly owned subsidiary of LG Electronics, serving as LG''s U.S. research subsidiary for consumer electronics, hospitality, health care technologies, and broadcasting standards.

Today, Zenith functions as a technology development and licensing organization. Its researchers create encryption and broadcast technologies, most notably Pro:Idiom, a digital television encryption system widely deployed in the hospitality industry. The company administers licensing for Pro:Idiom, offering royalty-free agreements to qualified partners.

Zenith''s technologies serve the consumer electronics, hospitality, health care, and broadcasting sectors. Hotel operators and digital TV providers implement Pro:Idiom to secure premium content delivery. The company''s broadcast standards work supports terrestrial HDTV transmission, while its health care and consumer electronics research feeds into LG''s global product lines.

The Zenith name has been associated with electronics innovation since 1918. Company records cite a legacy of firsts: the first wireless TV remote control, the first portable and push-button radios, the first stereo audio systems for FM radio and television, and the first terrestrial broadcast system for HDTV using digital technology. That heritage of pioneering standards continues to drive its licensing and research mission.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Technology development", "Licensing", "Research and development", "Encryption technology (Pro:Idiom)", "Consumer electronics research", "Hospitality technology", "Health care technology", "Broadcasting standards development", "Hotel Internet Services"], "industries": ["Consumer electronics", "Hospitality", "Health care", "Broadcasting"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Pro:Idiom encryption technology for hospitality digital TV signals", "Royalty-free licensing for qualified partners", "Over 100 years of electronics innovation heritage", "Pioneered first wireless TV remote, portable radios, stereo audio, and HDTV broadcast system"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1918 -> db", "Headquartered in Lincolnshire, Illinois -> db", "Wholly owned subsidiary of LG Electronics since 1999 -> db", "Technology development and licensing company -> db", "Created Pro:Idiom encryption technology for hospitality -> /", "Licensing administered with royalty-free agreements -> /", "Pioneered first wireless TV remote, portable radios, stereo audio, HDTV broadcast system -> /", "Serves consumer electronics, hospitality, health care, broadcasting industries -> /"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Zenith Electronics LLC a leading U.S. technology development and licensing company.", "founded_year": "1918", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='zenith-electronics-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Zenith Systems operates from Bedford Heights, Ohio, as an electrical and technology construction and design organization. The company traces its roots to the electrical construction industry, though a founding year and original founders are not publicly disclosed. Ownership details are not specified.

The firm delivers a full suite of electrical and low‑voltage services, including electrical construction, design‑build engineering, teledata infrastructure, audio/video integration, security system design and installation, fire alarm and life‑safety systems, and ongoing 24/7/365 maintenance. Its engineering group handles complex projects using state‑of‑the‑art design techniques, while field teams execute installations ranging from simple lighting retrofits to the electrical and technology backbone of half‑million‑square‑foot healthcare facilities.

Zenith serves a broad set of verticals: healthcare, education, industrial, energy and renewables, data centers, transportation, government, historic renovation, commercial, and utilities. Notable projects include work at Tripoint Medical Center and the St. John Medical Center modernization.

The company emphasizes a “one‑stop partner” model, combining more than 200 years of collective security experience, recognition as a top‑50 U.S. integrator, and award‑winning audio/video engineering. A 24‑hour emergency service line and a quality management system embedded in every project phase are cited as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical construction", "Design\u2011build engineering", "Teledata / structured cabling", "Audio/video system integration", "Security system design and installation", "Fire alarm and life\u2011safety systems", "Electrical engineering design", "Project management", "24/7/365 maintenance and service", "Energy management systems", "Voice and data networking"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Education", "Industrial", "Energy and Renewables", "Data Centers", "Transportation", "Government", "Historic Renovation", "Commercial", "Utilities"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["24\u2011hour emergency service line", "Single\u2011source responsibility for electrical, technology, and life\u2011safety systems", "Over 200 years of combined security integration experience", "Recognized as a top\u201150 systems integrator in the U.S.", "Award\u2011winning audio/video design\u2011build capability"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Bedford Heights, Ohio -> db", "Services: electrical construction, design-build, teledata, audio/video, security, fire alarm, engineering design -> /", "Markets served: healthcare, education, industrial, energy and renewables, data centers, transportation, government, historic renovation, commercial, utilities -> /about-us", "Specific projects: Tripoint Medical Center, St. John Medical Center Modernization -> db", "24-hour emergency service line -> /", "Collective security experience: over 200 years -> /", "Top 50 integrator recognition -> /", "Award-winning audio/video engineers -> /", "Quality management embed