UPDATE companies SET description='8th Avenue Food & Provisions is headquartered in Minneapolis, Minnesota. The company was founded in 2018 through the strategic combination of Post Holdings'' private-brands businesses, creating a dedicated platform for private-label and branded food manufacturing. In 2025, Post Holdings completed its acquisition of 8th Avenue and merged it with the Post Consumer Brands segment, while the company''s pasta business — formerly Dakota Growers Pasta Co. — was transferred to Richardson Food & Ingredients effective December 1, 2025.

The company produces nut butters, granola, dried fruits, nuts, and trail mixes across seven facilities in the United States and Canada. Plants in Fitzgerald, Georgia; Troy, Alabama; Blaine, Washington; Markham, Ontario; and Brampton, Ontario focus on nut butter. A Eugene, Oregon site makes granola, and a Hazelwood, Missouri facility handles fruits and nuts. 8th Avenue describes itself as one of the largest private-label nut butter manufacturers in North America, with in-house roasting and seasoning capabilities and decades of production experience.

Its customer base spans retail, food-service, and ingredient channels. The company supplies private-label programs for national and regional brands, providing custom formulations that include organic and non-GMO granola options as well as conventional and organic peanut and tree-nut butters.

8th Avenue emphasizes a rigorous supplier-approval program, food-safety systems, and supply-chain efficiency as its operational differentiators. The business was created to give brand owners a single source for on-trend, high-quality private-label foods backed by responsive service.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Nut butter manufacturing", "Granola production", "In-house nut roasting", "In-house seasoning", "Trail mix blending", "Dried fruit processing", "Private-label co-manufacturing", "Custom formulation development", "Organic certification compliance", "Non-GMO project compliance"], "industries": ["Retail", "Food service", "Ingredient manufacturing", "Private-label brands"], "materials": ["Peanuts", "Tree nuts", "Dried fruits", "Grains", "Organic ingredients", "Non-GMO ingredients"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One of the largest private-label nut butter manufacturers in North America", "In-house roasting and seasoning for nuts and trail mixes", "Rigorous supplier-approval program for ingredient safety", "Organic and non-GMO granola capabilities", "Seven production sites across the U.S. and Canada"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2018 through strategic combination of Post Holdings'' private brands businesses -> /", "Headquartered in Minneapolis, Minnesota -> db", "Manufactures nut butters, granola, dried fruits, nuts, trail mix -> /", "Operates 7 facilities across US and Canada -> /", "One of largest private-label nut butter manufacturers in North America -> /", "In-house roasting and seasoning processes -> /", "Serves retail, food service, ingredient sectors -> /", "Pasta business sold to Richardson Food & Ingredients effective December 1, 2025 -> /", "Rigorous supplier approval program for food safety -> /", "Organic and non-GMO granola options -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As a leading manufacturer of private-brand and branded foods, we craft nut butters, granola, dried fruits, nuts and trail mix products", "founded_year": "2018", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='8th-avenue-food-and-provisions-dakota-growers-pasta-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='A & H Metals Inc. is a family-owned and operated custom metal shop based in Newark, Delaware. The company was founded in 1971 and has been fabricating and installing metalwork for over five decades.

The shop specializes in sheet metal fabrication and welding, producing architectural railing systems with glass, perforated infill, and cable designs, as well as miscellaneous metal fabrications such as canopies, gates, stairs, and railings. It also delivers architectural facade systems using aluminum composite (ACM), high-pressure laminate (HPL), phenolic, insulated metal panels (IMP), fiber cement, and living wall systems. A custom fab shop with specialized machinery handles custom metal structures and products tailored to client specifications.

A & H Metals serves architects, structural fabricators, high-end builders, industrial plant managers, general contractors, and designers. Notable projects include work for Longwood Gardens, the University of Delaware’s Caesar Rodney Dining Hall Complex, and projects with The Whiting-Turner Contracting Company and EDiS Company.

